{
    "type": "Collection",
    "id": "AAS_4144_TEM_1",
    "stac_version": "1.1.0",
    "description": "This archive includes TEM images and spectroscopy of particles from an ice core from Law Dome, East Antarctica (DSS 05/06). The images are organized into three folders labelled 1795, 1838, and 1930 Common Era (C.E.). These dates correspond with the mean age of the meter of ice core melted for sampling. The depth/age scale of the ice core was constructed by matching dissolved ion chemistry and water stable isotope records (d18O) to the main DSS ice core record. which was dated using annual layer counting and validated by well-characterized volcanic horizons [Plummer et al., 2012].\n\nTEM images and corresponding EDS/EELS spectra are organized into subfolders by assigned particle ID.",
